    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d251-a1">

                <pb facs="0519" n="385" xml:id="pg385"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Messrs Tsan and Bee to Mr. Vincent</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chinese Consulate-General</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">San
                                Francisco, Cal.</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1887-07-14"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 14, 1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: Referring to this case-of the Chinese
                    subjects recently murdered on Snake River, this consulate is desirous of
                    obtaining further information.</p>
                <p>We beg therefore to ask your good offices in giving us such information as you
                    have in regard to the outrage. If not in your province to do so, will you kindly
                    refer this letter to any one who can enlighten us further than what we have seen
                    in the press dispatches, which merely announced the finding of the bodies of
                    several Chinese in the river?</p>
                <p>We have the honor, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed>
                        <list>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Liang Ting Tsan</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Consul-General</hi>.</item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. A. Bee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Consul.</hi></item>
                        </list>
                    </signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
